                      (    forth6809.asm):04509                                   ; UNLOOP discarding 6 of the 8 bytes itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):04510                                   ; then EXITUNLOOP unconditionally discarding
                      (    forth6809.asm):04511                                   ; a full 8 more, overshooting into whatever
                      (    forth6809.asm):04512                                   ; sat below (typically the caller's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):04513                                   ; return address) and branching into random
                      (    forth6809.asm):04514                                   ; memory on return. Since UNLOOP has no
                      (    forth6809.asm):04515                                   ; other legitimate use than immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):04516                                   ; preceding an exit from the definition, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):04517                                   ; EXIT already handles that correctly on its
                      (    forth6809.asm):04518                                   ; own, UNLOOP is now a true no-op rather than
