F725 3706             (    forth6809.asm):06596         UNESCAPEW: PULU D        ; BUG FIX: was PULU D/STD UESRCLEN (storing
F727 DDAB             (    forth6809.asm):06597                    STD  UEDST     ; the popped dest-addr into the SOURCE-
                      (    forth6809.asm):06598                                   ; length variable), then LDD ,U (a PEEK, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):06599                                   ; a pop) into BOTH UEADDR and UEDST - so the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06600                                   ; real source length was misread as an
                      (    forth6809.asm):06601                                   ; address, the real source address was never
                      (    forth6809.asm):06602                                   ; popped at all, and the true destination
                      (    forth6809.asm):06603                                   ; address never reached UEDST. Correct
                      (    forth6809.asm):06604                                   ; ANS order is ( c-addr1 u1 c-addr2 -- ):
                      (    forth6809.asm):06605                                   ; c-addr2 (dest) is on top, popped first.
F729 3706             (    forth6809.asm):06606                    PULU D         ; next: u1 (source length)
F72B DDA9             (    forth6809.asm):06607                    STD  UESRCLEN
F72D 3706             (    forth6809.asm):06608                    PULU D         ; next: c-addr1 (source address)
F72F DDA7             (    forth6809.asm):06609                    STD  UEADDR
F731 CC0000           (    forth6809.asm):06610                    LDD  #0
F734 DDAD             (    forth6809.asm):06611                    STD  UEOUTLEN
F736 9EA7             (    forth6809.asm):06612                    LDX  UEADDR
F738 109EAB           (    forth6809.asm):06613                    LDY  UEDST
                      (    forth6809.asm):06614         
                      (    forth6809.asm):06615                    ; ALGORITHM REPLACED (caught by MAME testing after the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06616                    ; argument-order fix above): the entire body below used
                      (    forth6809.asm):06617                    ; to decode backslash escape sequences (\n, \t, \\, \") -
                      (    forth6809.asm):06618                    ; a plausible-looking but entirely wrong reading of what
                      (    forth6809.asm):06619                    ; ANS UNESCAPE does. Confirmed against the actual spec and
                      (    forth6809.asm):06620                    ; its canonical reference implementation (forth-standard.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06621                    ; org/standard/string/UNESCAPE and complang.tuwien.ac.at's
                      (    forth6809.asm):06622                    ; ANS Forth reference text): UNESCAPE has nothing to do
                      (    forth6809.asm):06623                    ; with backslash sequences at all - it replaces every '%'
                      (    forth6809.asm):06624                    ; character with two '%' characters, and nothing else, so
                      (    forth6809.asm):06625                    ; that a literal '%' in text survives an eventual
                      (    forth6809.asm):06626                    ; SUBSTITUTE pass unchanged ("If you pass a string through
                      (    forth6809.asm):06627                    ; UNESCAPE and then SUBSTITUTE, you get the original
                      (    forth6809.asm):06628                    ; string"). Every character that ISN'T '%' passes straight
                      (    forth6809.asm):06629                    ; through, one-for-one. Confirmed via MAME: doubling a
                      (    forth6809.asm):06630                    ; single '%' wasn't happening at all, and the returned
                      (    forth6809.asm):06631                    ; count didn't grow to reflect the added characters -
                      (    forth6809.asm):06632                    ; both are direct, expected consequences of this being the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06633                    ; wrong algorithm entirely, not a smaller bug within it.
F73B DCA9             (    forth6809.asm):06634         UELOOP:    LDD  UESRCLEN
F73D 2715             (    forth6809.asm):06635                    BEQ  UEDONE
F73F A680             (    forth6809.asm):06636                    LDA  ,X+
F741 8125             (    forth6809.asm):06637                    CMPA #'%'
F743 2604             (    forth6809.asm):06638                    BNE  UENOTPCT
F745 C625             (    forth6809.asm):06639                    LDB  #'%'      ; write the extra '%' first - the character
F747 E7A0             (    forth6809.asm):06640                    STB  ,Y+       ; itself still gets written once more below,
                      (    forth6809.asm):06641                                   ; giving two '%' total for each one in the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06642                                   ; source. Handles multiple '%' characters in
                      (    forth6809.asm):06643                                   ; the same string correctly, since this runs
                      (    forth6809.asm):06644                                   ; independently for each one the loop visits.
F749 A7A0             (    forth6809.asm):06645         UENOTPCT:  STA  ,Y+       ; write the actual character - always, for
                      (    forth6809.asm):06646                                   ; every character, '%' or not
F74B DCA9             (    forth6809.asm):06647                    LDD  UESRCLEN
F74D 830001           (    forth6809.asm):06648                    SUBD #1
F750 DDA9             (    forth6809.asm):06649                    STD  UESRCLEN
F752 20E7             (    forth6809.asm):06650                    BRA  UELOOP
F754 1F20             (    forth6809.asm):06651         UEDONE:    TFR  Y,D       ; BUG FIX: was "LDD UEOUTLEN / STD ,U" -
F756 93AB             (    forth6809.asm):06652                    SUBD UEDST     ; overwriting whatever was left on top of
F758 DDAD             (    forth6809.asm):06653                    STD  UEOUTLEN  ; the stack rather than pushing both
                      (    forth6809.asm):06654                                   ; required return values, and separately,
                      (    forth6809.asm):06655                                   ; UEOUTLEN itself was never correctly
                      (    forth6809.asm):06656                                   ; tracked by the old backslash-decoding
                      (    forth6809.asm):06657                                   ; loop's own per-character bookkeeping in a
                      (    forth6809.asm):06658                                   ; way that accounted for doubled '%'
                      (    forth6809.asm):06659                                   ; characters. Now computed directly as the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06660                                   ; final write pointer (Y) minus the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06661                                   ; original destination address (UEDST) -
                      (    forth6809.asm):06662                                   ; correct regardless of how many characters
                      (    forth6809.asm):06663                                   ; were doubled, since it's derived from
                      (    forth6809.asm):06664                                   ; where writing actually stopped rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):06665                                   ; incremented alongside it.
F75A DCAB             (    forth6809.asm):06666                    LDD  UEDST
F75C 3606             (    forth6809.asm):06667                    PSHU D         ; push c-addr2 (destination address)
F75E DCAD             (    forth6809.asm):06668                    LDD  UEOUTLEN
F760 3606             (    forth6809.asm):06669                    PSHU D         ; push u2 (actual unescaped length)
F762 39               (    forth6809.asm):06670                    RTS
                      (    forth6809.asm):06671         
                      (    forth6809.asm):06672         ; REPLACES/SUBSTITUTE - single-slot simplified version, per
                      (    forth6809.asm):06673         ; the explicit scoping-down discussed in the source conversation
F763 3706             (    forth6809.asm):06674         REPLACESW: PULU D
F765 DDB5             (    forth6809.asm):06675                    STD  REPLNLEN
F767 3706             (    forth6809.asm):06676                    PULU D
