                      (    forth6809.asm):07283         ; ENVIRONMENT? - dispatcher complete; table has entries derived
                      (    forth6809.asm):07284         ; without fabricating unfixed capacities. /HOLD and /PAD were both
                      (    forth6809.asm):07285         ; added this session, answering HOLDMINSIZE and PADMINSIZE
                      (    forth6809.asm):07286         ; respectively (see each entry itself, below, for why each uses its
                      (    forth6809.asm):07287         ; own, conceptually correct constant rather than the numerically-
                      (    forth6809.asm):07288         ; equal PADOFFSET).
                      (    forth6809.asm):07289         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):07290         ; WORDLISTS (16.3.2, Search-Order word set) is deliberately absent
                      (    forth6809.asm):07291         ; from ENVTABLE, not an oversight - this system doesn't implement
                      (    forth6809.asm):07292         ; the Search-Order word set, so WORDLISTS is genuinely an unknown
                      (    forth6809.asm):07293         ; attribute here. Per ENVIRONMENT?'s own spec (6.1.1345): "If the
                      (    forth6809.asm):07294         ; system treats the attribute as unknown, the returned flag is
                      (    forth6809.asm):07295         ; false" - falling through to ENVNOTFOUND already produces exactly
                      (    forth6809.asm):07296         ; that, correctly and completely, with no dispatcher work needed.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07297         ; Confirmed via MAME testing.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07298         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):07299         ; MAX-D/MAX-UD were resolved this session via a genuine dispatcher
                      (    forth6809.asm):07300         ; extension, not just a table entry - both are double-cell values
                      (    forth6809.asm):07301         ; per their own ANS data type, which the original single-cell
                      (    forth6809.asm):07302         ; ENVFOUND (pushing exactly one value before TRUE) couldn't
                      (    forth6809.asm):07303         ; represent. Added a second table (ENVTABLE2) and matching loop
                      (    forth6809.asm):07304         ; (ENV2START/ENV2LOOP/ENV2FOUND, below) specifically for double-cell
                      (    forth6809.asm):07305         ; entries, rather than reworking the single-cell path to handle both
                      (    forth6809.asm):07306         ; shapes - see those labels for the full design.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07307         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):07308         ; FLOORED was the third, separate open item flagged previously -
                      (    forth6809.asm):07309         ; investigated this session by tracing DIVCOMMON (shared by /, MOD,
                      (    forth6809.asm):07310         ; /MOD) against this system's own SM/REM and FM/MOD. Confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):07311         ; DIVCOMMON matches SM/REM's convention exactly (remainder sign
                      (    forth6809.asm):07312         ; restored from the dividend's own original sign, not the quotient's)
                      (    forth6809.asm):07313         ; - this system's primary division words use symmetric division, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):07314         ; floored. FLOORED now answers 0 (false) - see the entry itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):07315         ; below, for the full trace.
FB88 3706             (    forth6809.asm):07316         ENVQUERY: PULU D
FB8A DDEF             (    forth6809.asm):07317                   STD  ENVLEN
FB8C 3706             (    forth6809.asm):07318                   PULU D
FB8E DDF1             (    forth6809.asm):07319                   STD  ENVADDR
FB90 8EFC23           (    forth6809.asm):07320                   LDX  #ENVTABLE
FB93 EC84             (    forth6809.asm):07321         ENVLOOP:  LDD  ,X
FB95 10830000         (    forth6809.asm):07322                   CMPD #0
FB99 272B             (    forth6809.asm):07323                   BEQ  ENV2START  ; CHANGED: was BEQ ENVNOTFOUND - now tries
                      (    forth6809.asm):07324                                     ; the double-cell table (below) before
                      (    forth6809.asm):07325                                     ; giving up entirely. See ENV2START/
                      (    forth6809.asm):07326                                     ; ENV2LOOP for MAX-D/MAX-UD, added this
                      (    forth6809.asm):07327                                     ; turn - both are double-cell values per
                      (    forth6809.asm):07328                                     ; their own ANS data type, which this
                      (    forth6809.asm):07329                                     ; single-cell table's ENVFOUND (pushing
                      (    forth6809.asm):07330                                     ; exactly one value before TRUE) can't
                      (    forth6809.asm):07331                                     ; represent correctly.
FB9B 3410             (    forth6809.asm):07332                   PSHS X          ; BUG FIX: COMPAREW uses X as its own
                      (    forth6809.asm):07333                                     ; internal scratch (LDX CMPA1, then LDA
                      (    forth6809.asm):07334                                     ; ,X+ advancing through the comparison),
                      (    forth6809.asm):07335                                     ; clobbering whatever the caller had there.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07336                                     ; ENVQUERY needs X to still point at the
                      (    forth6809.asm):07337                                     ; current table entry after COMPAREW
                      (    forth6809.asm):07338                                     ; returns, both for ENVFOUND's own LDD 4,X
                      (    forth6809.asm):07339                                     ; and for advancing to the next entry -
                      (    forth6809.asm):07340                                     ; without saving it first, a successful
